    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457-a1">

                <pb facs="0889" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg765"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1, in No. 208.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Mariscal to Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In consequence of your excellency’s note,
                    dated the 27th of January last, relative to the complaints of citizens of the
                    United States who trade with Mexico, and who affirm they have been molested by
                    employés of the custom-houses of different ports of the republic, I have the
                    honor to transmit to your excellency, with the present note, a copy of an
                    official communication on this subject, dated 19th instant, which was addressed
                    to me by the secretary of the treasury.</p>
                <p>I renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>IGNACIO MARISCAL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
